Two files under test/fixtures/ are not. They are signed archives taken from
webrecorder/py-wacz, kept because they are the only signatures in this
repository that capping did not produce itself:

  test/fixtures/pywacz-signed.datapackage-digest.json
  test/fixtures/pywacz-signed-invalid.datapackage-digest.json

Derived from:
  https://github.com/webrecorder/py-wacz
  (wacz/tests/fixtures — signed with authsigner 0.3.0 in 2022)

They are what makes the verifier measurable against something outside this
project. Without them, capping's tests would only show that its signer and its
verifier agree with each other, which they would do just as happily if both
had misread the format.

